## TokenLighten

Use TL for unknown-location, multi-file/call-graph or large-file work.
FIRST for every request, including unanchored natural-language questions: `tl_read_file {"cwd":"<workspace>","query":"<entire user request, verbatim>","task":{"epoch":"new"}}`; preserve constraints/citations. Read-only question: task.profile:"answer"; requested changes/fixes: "generic" (mixed=>generic); otherwise omit. Omit unknown targets. Use native tools for a user-named file with a small local task, if requested, TL unavailable/native-bypass, its result is unusable, or scope is incomplete/absent; return to TL when usable.
Every call: top-level cwd; add no cwd to a next. Working alone, omit lane. In parallel, set it on call 1 and never change it. Same request's later calls: returned task.id as task.handle, never epoch:"new"; expected_state_version only beside handle.
Act on decision.kind: act.answer/act.edit => use exact evidence[].body and paths/lines without re-reading; if a required body is missing after act.answer, read that target; act.edit: same rule; later reads: targets[] (path|handle,range), no query. Batch independent reads: ONE targets[]; edits: ONE edits[]. Unknown kind => stop/report; never infer. Run next verbatim; hints are not calls. refusal.retry: call=>correct field; new-task=>re-pack; user-input=>ask; none=>stop. await_input: run next first; otherwise candidates are unverified: targeted find→outline→ranges; ask only if ambiguous.
read.receipt=>reuse served bodies/handles; follow next, else act/stop. Lost bodies: task.force_serve:true. task.pull:"closure" returns checks, not source: use only after an edit carries closure; omit when reading targets. Search: action:"find", one literal identifier per queries[] entry, never a phrase; scope.path if known; references=call sites, tree=listing; budgets: budget.bytes/tokens.
Path edits need no prior read: path/search/replace+precondition:"unique-match",allowPathFallback:false. Before editing, check code/tests and other spellings. Handle must cover search; multiple windows: prefer path. Create: path,create:true,content; empty frontier+create_target=>create. Writes require --allow-write. edit.applied=>landed; edit.rolled_back=>nothing landed; edit.state_unknown=>run recovery first. Never retry failed edits verbatim; operation_id replay is safe. Verification omitted=>run batched next before tests; discharge recipe.gaps. Shell: build/tests/git; native read/search/edit is allowed under the fallback conditions above. Stop after relevant checks pass.
